      "blob_url": "https://github.com/verl-project/verl/blob/be57fcc4168c829e39e2da0c9ef8c15c852ad633/verl%2Fmodel_merger%2Fmegatron_model_merger.py",
      "changes": 9,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/verl-project/verl/contents/verl%2Fmodel_merger%2Fmegatron_model_merger.py?ref=be57fcc4168c829e39e2da0c9ef8c15c852ad633",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "verl/model_merger/megatron_model_merger.py",
      "patch": "@@ -364,12 +364,21 @@ def _validate_state_dict(self, state_dict: dict[str, torch.Tensor]):\n             torch.testing.assert_close(loaded_weight.to(\"cpu\"), param, atol=1e-2, rtol=5e-2)\n \n     def _replace_name(self, megatron_name: str, name_mapping: dict[str, str]) -> str:\n+        def convert_name_fast(old_name):\n+            parts = old_name.split('.')\n+            left_half = \".\".join(parts[:5])\n+            right_half = parts[5]\n+            expert_idx = parts[-1].replace(\"weight\", \"\")  \n+            new_name = f\"{left_half}.{expert_idx}.{right_half}.weight\"\n+            return new_name\n         for m_name, v_name in name_mapping.items():\n             if m_name not in megatron_name:\n                 continue\n \n             megatron_name = megatron_name.replace(\"decoder\", \"model\")\n             param_name = megatron_name.replace(m_name, v_name)\n+            if \"mlp.experts\" in param_name:\n+                param_name = convert_name_fast(param_name)\n             return param_name\n \n         return None  # Return None if no mapping found",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/verl-project/verl/raw/be57fcc4168c829e39e2da0c9ef8c15c852ad633/verl%2Fmodel_merger%2Fmegatron_model_merger.py",
      "sha": "e5b78cf00c7a0a874959d9e486cfef43c9e5ba9f",
      "status": "modified"
    }
  ],
  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nThis nested function `convert_name_fast` is only used once within the scope of `_replace_name`. Consider removing the nested function and placing its logic directly within the `_replace_name` function to reduce unnecessary indentation and improve readability. This simplifies the code and makes it easier to follow the logic flow. Also, the variable name `old_name` is not very descriptive. Consider renaming it to `param_name` to better reflect its purpose and improve code clarity.\n\n```python\n        parts = megatron_name.split('.')\n        left_half = \".\".join(parts[:5])\n        right_half = parts[5]\n        expert_idx = parts[-1].replace(\"weight\", \"\")  \n        param_name = f\"{left_half}.{expert_idx}.{right_half}.weight\"\n\n```",
      "created_at": "2025-07-09T16:10:52Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -364,12 +364,21 @@ def _validate_state_dict(self, state_dict: dict[str, torch.Tensor]):\n             torch.testing.assert_close(loaded_weight.to(\"cpu\"), param, atol=1e-2, rtol=5e-2)\n \n     def _replace_name(self, megatron_name: str, name_mapping: dict[str, str]) -> str:\n+        def convert_name_fast(old_name):\n+            parts = old_name.split('.')\n+            left_half = \".\".join(parts[:5])\n+            right_half = parts[5]\n+            expert_idx = parts[-1].replace(\"weight\", \"\")  \n+            new_name = f\"{left_half}.{expert_idx}.{right_half}.weight\"\n+            return new_name",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pull/2444#discussion_r2195426541",
